## 9. AUTH — MULTI-USER GOOGLE (PKCE + LOOPBACK)

Same flow as before: Rust generates verifier, opens system browser, loopback listener on `127.0.0.1:PORT`, exchanges code, stores tokens in Stronghold, returns `{sub, email, name, picture}` to frontend.

Scopes:

- Personal: `openid email profile drive.appdata`
- Shared: `openid email profile drive.file`

`users.google_sub` is the stable ID. Never key on email. Sign-out revokes token via `POST /revoke` and clears Stronghold.

**PIN lock:** optional 4–6 digit PIN gates app on launch. Auto-lock after 5 min idle (configurable).

