### 11.13 Messengers Hub — NEW (deep links, not iframes)

**Why this changed:** WhatsApp, Telegram, and Discord **block embedding** in iframes (the "Refused to Connect" error). This is permanent and unfixable — it's their security policy. **Do not use iframes. Use deep links.**

**What the Messenger tab does:**

- Clean header with three tabs: WhatsApp, Telegram, Discord.
- Each tab shows a clean card: platform icon, "Open WhatsApp Desktop" button, "Open WhatsApp Web" button.
- Clicking **Open Desktop** uses Tauri's `opener::open_url('whatsapp://')` — launches the native app if installed.
- Clicking **Open Web** opens the default browser to `web.whatsapp.com` (or the equivalent) — never inside the app.
- Same for Telegram (`tg://` / `web.telegram.org/a/`) and Discord (`discord://` / `discord.com/app`).
- Above the cards, a **Quick Send** box: pick tenant from a dropdown, pick template, and the app generates the deep link with the message pre-filled:

- WhatsApp: `https://wa.me/<phone>?text=<encoded message>`
- SMS: `sms:<phone>?body=<encoded message>`
- Email: `mailto:<email>?subject=...&body=...`
- The quick-send box works while offline (generates the link) but opening the link requires network for WhatsApp Web. If offline, show a soft toast: "Message link copied — open when online."
- If the native app isn't installed, `opener::open_url` fails gracefully → fall back to browser URL.

### 11.14 Map — MapLibre GL + satellite + persistence

**Why MapLibre:** real streets, real buildings, satellite imagery, terrain — all free with no API keys.

**Layers available (tab switcher):**

- **Streets** — OpenStreetMap raster tiles (`https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png`)
- **Satellite** — Esri World Imagery (`https://server.arcgisonline.com/ArcGIS/rest/services/World_Imagery/MapServer/tile/{z}/{y}/{x}`)
- **Terrain** — OpenTopoMap (`https://a.tile.opentopomap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png`)

**Features:**

- Property pins from lat/lng stored on each property
- Click pin → info card with property name, address, "Copy address", "Copy coordinates", "Open in system maps"
- Click empty map area → "Add property here" flow (pre-fills lat/lng)
- Search box: type city/region → fly to that location (uses free Nominatim search — no key)